name w5-baltic-qra
time 2018-01-15T10:00:00Z
carry units ground stores
stop_on never

# CAMPAIGN W5 - BALTIC AIR POLICING / QRA: IDENTIFICATION AS THE TASK.
# Spec, anchor, sources and disputes: doc/campaigns/w5-baltic-qra.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
#
# THE FIRST CAMPAIGN OF THE FIVE IN WHICH THE F-16 FLIES, AND THE ONLY ONE OF THE TEN WHOSE SUCCESS
# CONDITION CONTAINS NO WEAPON. The task is to put eyes on an unknown aeroplane and say what it is:
# presence, identification, escort - not combat. In eight of the ten sorties a weapon release is a
# FAILURE and not a result, and in the other two it is a failure with a declared exception that no file
# exercises.
#
# THE QUESTION THIS CAMPAIGN ASKS IS NOT "DOES THE INTERCEPT SUCCEED". It is: WHAT DOES AN
# IDENTIFICATION COST, AND WHAT IS THE TREE ACTUALLY ABLE TO IDENTIFY? Four currencies, all measured:
# TIME (spawn to `mission IDENTIFIED`), FUEL (the column at three ticks), PROXIMITY (closest approach
# in metres) and RISK (who is painting you while you fly the box). Sortie 05 is the file that prices
# all four in one run; the other nine hold three of them fixed and move one thing.
#
# AND THE SECOND HALF, WHICH IS OLDER THAN THIS CAMPAIGN: IDENTITY IS THE SHARPEST AVAILABLE TEST OF
# THE ANTI-CHEAT BOUNDARY. An AI that cheats about shooting is hard to catch, because a fast accurate
# kill can be good flying. An AI that cheats about IDENTITY is caught in one diff, because the correct
# behaviour toward an unknown is the same whatever it turns out to be. Sorties 01/02/03 are that
# experiment on the western airframe, and O2's `o2-06/07/08` are its eastern twin.
#
# THE THREE-FILE RULE, BUDGETED IN ADVANCE. Rule 10 (O2): a byte-identical pair has two possible
# causes - no leak, or a dead channel - so it needs a control run in which the channel demonstrably
# fires. O2 built the pair and added the third file afterwards; this campaign budgets the third slot
# before writing the first file, and the three are sorties 01, 02 and 03.
#
# TEMPORAL HONESTY: NONE NEEDED, AND THAT IS UNUSUAL IN THIS SET. F-16s of several NATO air forces have
# flown Baltic Air Policing rotations since 2004 and the mission is current [T4]; the flying jet is the
# jet. What IS substituted is the SUBJECT, and in the direction that makes the campaign HARDER to
# dismiss rather than easier: the real subject is an Il-20 ELINT aircraft, an An-26 or a Tu-95, and
# FlightBox now has two of those three as catalogue MOVER rows. W5's own spec calls this campaign
# blocked on gap C7; rule 7 says re-check the CAPABILITY against the tree, and the capability is there,
# because a mover needs no generated deck and the `ALPHA` verdict is about decks.
#
# THE CLOCK is a JANUARY Baltic rotation: 10:00 Z (12:00 local, sun ~11 deg up) for the seven day
# sorties and 20:00 Z for the two night ones plus the capstone. Why not June, which is when Baltic
# incidents are most reported: at 55.9 N the sun's elevation at midsummer solar midnight is
# lat + dec - 90 = -10.7 deg [DERIVED], barely below the -9 deg nautical-twilight floor the daylight
# term uses, so a June "night" would be a marginal reading of a threshold rather than a night. Every
# mission declares its own `time`, so the campaign clock above never has to fill one in.
# THE GROUND is `--elev const` on a 0 m datum, and every fingerprint below is comparable only against
# runs whose campaign-summary.txt records `elev const`.
#
# CALLSIGN AND CARRY TOPOLOGY, STATED BEFORE THE FIRST MISSION FILE:
#   ALL TEN CASTS ARE PAIRWISE DISJOINT, aircraft AND ground (`q1*` .. `q9*`, `qa*`). Nothing is
#   carried in or out of any sortie, and there is NO CHAIN in this campaign.
#
# WHY THERE IS NO CHAIN, AND WHY THE CARRY IS NEVERTHELESS DECLARED UNNARROWED. Rule 2 says the carry
# belongs where the campaign has a QUESTION about it. This one has none: nothing here shoots, so no
# unit is lost, no ground object is touched and no store is expended. A chain would carry three empty
# facts and buy a slot's worth of nothing. But the carry is NOT narrowed either, because the campaign's
# own discipline is exactly what an unnarrowed carry measures at campaign scope: `campaign ATTRITION`
# and `campaign EXPENDED` over ten sorties are the aggregate `no_fire` proof, computed by the runner
# and not by the reader. A rotation in which every one of those numbers is zero is the machine-checked
# statement that the hold held. THE PRICE, STATED: THIS CAMPAIGN SHOWS NO ATTRITION ARC AND CANNOT.
#
# THE TEN SORTIES AND THE ONE CHANGE EACH MAKES - each file's own header carries its binding reading
# rule (doc/missions/INDEX.md rule 5) and this list is the campaign's index only:
#   01 cooperative     the subject answers                                <- CONTROL RUN of 03
#   02 silent          [ctrl 01] it does not answer                       <- control of 03, 08, 09
#   03 team-swap       [ctrl 02] ONE token: the subject's `team`          <- THE ANTI-CHEAT PAIR
#   04 escorted        a bomber with two fighter escorts, three contacts, two interceptors
#   05 shadow          a 40 km run-down, a 120 s hold and a wind - the file that prices the task
#   06 two-subjects    two subjects, two interceptors, one sort
#   07 locked-on       the subject paints you, and you are armed
#   08 weather-id      [ctrl 02] ONE line: `wx fixture`
#   09 night-id        [ctrl 02] ONE line: the hour of `time`
#   10 alpha           night + cloud + bomber + escorts that radiate + four jets: the capstone
#
# THREE ATTRIBUTION RUNS ARE NOT PART OF THE TEN and live in doc/campaigns/w5-baltic-qra.md, State:
#   A1  sortie 02's geometry with `set task intercept` - what the pilot AI does with this task
#   A2  sortie 05 with `wx calm` - the wind separated from the station-keeping
#   A3  sortie 08 with `wx wind 225 40` - the wind separated from the cloud (rule 4)
#
# READING RULE FOR THE CAMPAIGN. Unlike the four campaigns before it, this one's sorties mostly return
# a REAL verdict rather than a measuring rig's TIMEOUT: `objective identify` and `objective no_fire`
# (round C12) were built for exactly this task, so exit 0 means the pass was flown and no weapon left
# the aeroplane. THE CAMPAIGN EXIT IS THE WORST STEP'S. A FAIL (exit 1) anywhere is the campaign's most
# important result and is reported with the tick of the release; a TIMEOUT (exit 3) means an
# identification was briefed and not flown. Beside the code, read `campaign ATTRITION` and
# `campaign EXPENDED` - in this campaign they are the verdict on the discipline and both are expected
# to be zero.

mission ../missions/w5-01-cooperative.fbm
mission ../missions/w5-02-silent.fbm
mission ../missions/w5-03-team-swap.fbm
mission ../missions/w5-04-escorted.fbm
mission ../missions/w5-05-shadow.fbm
mission ../missions/w5-06-two-subjects.fbm
mission ../missions/w5-07-locked-on.fbm
mission ../missions/w5-08-weather-id.fbm
mission ../missions/w5-09-night-id.fbm
mission ../missions/w5-10-alpha.fbm
